We state the eight no-go theorems. Each theorem is followed by a brief remark clarifying scope.

\begin{theorem}[NG\_ARROW\_DPI]\label{thm:NG_ARROW_DPI}
\ThmStmtNGARROWDPI
\end{theorem}

expanded_source_wording_tex:
We state the eight no-go theorems. Each theorem is followed by a brief remark clarifying scope.

\begin{theorem}[NG\_ARROW\_DPI]\label{thm:NG_ARROW_DPI}
Let $\mu\in\Delta(\mathsf{X})$, let $P:\mathsf{X}\times\mathsf{X}\to[0,1]$ be row-stochastic, and let $T\ge 1$. Define the micro path law on $\mathsf{X}^{T+1}$ by \[\mathbf{P}^{(T)}_{\mu,P}(x_{0:T})=\mu(x_0)\prod_{t=0}^{T-1}P(x_t,x_{t+1}).\] Let $\mathrm{rev}_T(x_{0:T})=(x_T,\dots,x_0)$ and let $\ell:\mathsf{X}\to\mathsf{Y}$ be deterministic with pointwise extension $\ell^{(T)}(x_{0:T})=(\ell(x_0),\dots,\ell(x_T))$. Then \[\mathrm{KL}\!\Big((\ell^{(T)})_{\#}\mathbf{P}^{(T)}_{\mu,P}\ \Big\|\ (\mathrm{rev}_T)_{\#}(\ell^{(T)})_{\#}\mathbf{P}^{(T)}_{\mu,P}\Big)\ \le\ \mathrm{KL}\!\Big(\mathbf{P}^{(T)}_{\mu,P}\ \Big\|\ (\mathrm{rev}_T)_{\#}\mathbf{P}^{(T)}_{\mu,P}\Big).\]

\end{theorem}

source_wording_tex:
The remainder of the paper proceeds as follows.  \Cref{sec:aor-background}
sets up the mathematical entry point: scoped carriers, reflective
completion, least fixed points, well-founded discharge, and directed
colimits.  \Cref{sec:aor-problem-setup} defines PreSB carriers, their
morphisms, and the AOR full subcategory.  \Cref{sec:aor-methods}
constructs \(\ClSB\), states its universal property, and packages the
adjunction with the inclusion.  \Cref{sec:aor-primary-results} develops the
primary diagnostic layer: \(\XiSB\), the eight strata, the residual atlas,
the atom calculus, and the AOR-8 status catalogue.  \Cref{sec:aor-secondary-results}
builds discharge cascades and cascade-stable AOR.  \Cref{sec:aor-analysis}
adds refinement chains, asymptotic statuses, directed-colimit behavior, and
the hierarchy.  \Cref{sec:aor-formal-framework} summarizes the formal
companion boundary and narrowing ledger.  Finally, \Cref{sec:aor-discussion}
states the status, scope, and nonclaim boundary, and
\Cref{sec:aor-conclusion} summarizes the audit-closure meta-theory.
 \section{Background}\label{sec:aor-background}

